now to washington where president biden  has called vladimir putin a war criminal  for the very first time his comments  come amid a fierce debate over what kind  of aid to send to ukraine following a  speech by ukrainian president vladimir  zelinsky to the united states congress  nancy cordes has more from the white  house i think he is a warframe  the white house says president biden was  quote speaking from the heart about  vladimir putin's barbaric actions when  he made that declaration it came after  weeks of the white house carefully  skirting the term war criminal  as the state department investigates  putin's spokesperson called the comment  unacceptable and unforgivable the world  is united in our support for ukraine  earlier in the day mr biden announced an  additional 800 million dollars  worth of military aid going straight  from the u.s to ukraine it includes 9  000 shoulder-mounted javelin missiles  800 stinger anti-aircraft systems and  more than 20 million rounds of  ammunition he's also giving ukraine  seven thousand grenade launchers more  guns and special anti-tank drones known  as switchblades i don't know where the  switchblade drone is but it sounds like  it should be going to the ukraine  but all that still does not fulfill the  top requests from ukrainian president  vladimir zelinsky being the leader of  the world means  to be the leader  of peace in an emotional appeal to  congress wednesday zielinski begged the  u.s to help impose a no-fly zone over  his country we're a superpower and  zielinski challenged us to act like it  but a no-fly zone is something neither  the white house nor most of congress  supports for fear it would draw u.s and  nato pilots into the conflict  i have a dream  these words are known to each of you  today i can say i have a need  i need to protect  our sky  as a fullback zelinski urged the u.s to  help him secure more mig-29 fighter jets  president biden should allow those migs  to go to ukraine today  behind the scenes u.s officials are  working to get zielenski something else  he's seeking s-300 russian-made  long-range surface-to-air missiles the  u.s doesn't have them but some eastern  european countries like bulgaria and  slovakia do vice president harris spoke  to the president of slovakia yesterday  and the defense secretary is set to  travel to both countries this week gail  all right nancy let's hope there's a lot  of behind the scenes conversations going  on that we're not aware of thank you so  much
 

